uction, see CA hierarchy and rotation. If you need to standardize what each authority can sign, use Certificate profiles."},"695":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-25","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#choose-a-flow","content":"**New CA with a new key:** create a root of trust from scratch. Lamassu generates and keeps the key pair."},"696":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-26","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#choose-a-flow","content":"**New CA from the KMS:** reuse a key already registered in the platform."},"697":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-27","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#choose-a-flow","content":"**Import a CA with its private key:** incorporate an external authority that Lamassu can issue with."},"698":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-28","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#choose-a-flow","content":"**Import only the certificate:** add an authority for building chains and validating, but not for issuing."},"699":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-29","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#choose-a-flow","content":"First time here? Follow Create your first CA to complete the minimal journey."},"700":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-30","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#before-you-begin","content":"Decide whether the CA will be a root or an intermediate."},"701":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-31","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#before-you-begin","content":"Choose the engine that will keep the key."},"702":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-32","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#before-you-begin","content":"Define a validity longer than that of the certificates it will issue."},"703":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-33","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#before-you-begin","content":"For an intermediate CA, make sure the parent CA is active."},"704":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-34","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#open-the-wizard","content":"In **Certification Authorities**, select **Create New CA** and choose to generate a new key pair."},"705":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-35","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#configure-the-key","content":"Select the cryptographic engine, the algorithm and the size or curve. Lamassu supports RSA and EC keys according to the engine's capabilities."},"706":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-36","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#configure-the-key","content":"For RSA you can choose 1024, 2048, 3072 or 4096 bits. For EC, the P-256, P-384 and P-521 curves are available."},"707":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-37","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#choose-the-ca-type","content":"Select **Root CA** for a self-signed authority or **Intermediate CA** for an authority signed by another CA. In the latter case, choose the issuing CA."},"708":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-38","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#define-the-identity","content":"Enter a unique **CA Name**. This name becomes the certificate's `Common Name`. Complete the Distinguished Name fields your policy requires:"},"709":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-39","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#define-the-identity","content":"`C`: two-letter ISO 3166-1 country code."},"710":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-40","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#define-the-identity","content":"`ST`: state or province."},"711":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-41","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#define-the-identity","content":"`L`: locality."},"712":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-42","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#define-the-identity","content":"`O`: organization."},"713":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-43","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#define-the-identity","content":"`OU`: organizational unit."},"714":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-44","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#define-the-identity","content":"The CA's internal identifier is generated automatically and cannot be changed."},"715":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-45","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#configure-validity-and-uses","content":"Define **CA Certificate Expiration** and **Default End-Entity Certificate Issuance Expiration**. You can express a duration (`5y 8w 4d`), pick a date or use the maximum allowed date."},"716":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-46","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#configure-validity-and-uses","content":"Select an existing issuance profile or configure the `Key Usage` and `Extended Key Usage` in the form. If you don't choose a profile, Lamassu applies the default basic usages."},"717":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-47","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#create-and-verify","content":"Confirm the form. The CA should appear in the inventory with its PEM certificate, status, expiration date and list of issued certificates."},"718":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-48","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#create-and-verify","content":"A CA cannot issue certificates that outlive its own expiration date. Leave enough margin to renew or replace the authority without interrupting consumers."},"719":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-49","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#use-a-key-from-the-kms","content":"Select &#x2A;*Create New CA (Existing Key)** when the key is already registered in Lamassu. The wizard first asks for the backing key and then shows the same configuration of type, identity, validity and profile."},"720":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-50","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/certificate-authorities#use-a-key-from-the-kms","content":"This flow is useful when the key was previously created in an HSM, imported through BYOK or must be reused under a specific custody policy."},"721":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/certificate-authorities-51","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/certificate-authorities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/certificate-authorit