#generate-a-csr","content":"**Country (C)**: two-letter country code."},"1645":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/key-management-110","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/key-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/key-management#generate-a-csr","content":"**State / Province (ST)**: state or province."},"1646":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/key-management-111","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/key-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/key-management#generate-a-csr","content":"**Locality (L)**: city or locality."},"1647":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/key-management-112","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/key-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/key-management#generate-a-csr","content":"**Email Address**: contact email."},"1648":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/key-management-113","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/key-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/key-management#generate-a-csr","content":"**Subject Alternative Names (SANs)**: alternative names or identifiers, such as DNS or IP."},"1649":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/key-management-114","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/key-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/key-management#generate-a-csr","content":"Once the form is complete, Lamassu generates the CSR and presents it for download or copy."},"1650":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/key-management-115","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/key-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/key-management#sign-locally-with-pkcs11","content":"Lamassu also offers specific help for local integrations through **Sign locally with OpenSSL & PKCS11 tools**."},"1651":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/key-management-116","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/key-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/key-management#sign-locally-with-pkcs11","content":"This option shows the steps needed to configure the local environment, load the PKCS#11 module and perform signatures with tools like OpenSSL without extracting the private key from the secured environment."},"1652":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/ocsp","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/ocsp","type":"page","content":"Online validation with OCSP","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Platform","Operate Lamassu"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/ocsp"},"1653":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/ocsp-0","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/ocsp","content":"Check in real time whether a certificate is still valid or has been revoked."},"1654":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/ocsp-1","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/ocsp","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/ocsp#ocsp-service","content":"OCSP service"},"1655":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/ocsp-2","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/ocsp","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/ocsp#how-the-responder-works-in-lamassu","content":"How the responder works in Lamassu"},"1656":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/ocsp-3","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/ocsp","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/ocsp#embedding-in-issued-certificates","content":"Embedding in issued certificates"},"1657":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/ocsp-4","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/ocsp","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/ocsp#http-endpoints","content":"HTTP endpoints"},"1658":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/ocsp-5","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/ocsp","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/ocsp#check-from-the-interface","content":"Check from the interface"},"1659":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/ocsp-6","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/ocsp","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/ocsp#references","content":"References"},"1660":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/ocsp-7","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/ocsp#ocsp-service","content":"OCSP (Online Certificate Status Protocol) is the mechanism that lets a relying party check, in real time, whether a specific certificate is valid or has been revoked. Instead of downloading a full list of revoked certificates, the client sends a query with the certificate's serial number and receives a signed response with the current status."},"1661":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/ocsp-8","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/ocsp#ocsp-service","content":"Lamassu integrates its own OCSP responder that serves these queries by consulting the internal certificate database directly. No external component is required."},"1662":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/ocsp-9","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/ocsp#how-the-responder-works-in-lamassu","content":"When a client requests the status of a certificate, the responder locates the certificate by its serial number and determines its status from the internal record:"},"1663":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/ocsp-10","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/ocsp#how-the-responder-works-in-lamassu","content":"If the certificate is active, the response indicates `Good`."},"1664":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/ocsp-11","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/ocsp#how-the-responder-works-in-lamassu","content":"If the certificate has been revoked, the response indicates `Revoked` and includes the revocation timestamp and the RFC 5280 reason code."},"1665":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/ocsp-12","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/ocsp#how-the-responder-works-in-lamassu","content":"If the serial number is not found or the status is not recognizable, the response indicates `Unknown`."},"1666":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/ocsp-13","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/ocsp#how-the-responder-works-in-lamassu","content":"The OCSP response is signed by the issuing CA of the queried certificate, using the cryptographic engine associated with that CA. Lamassu does not use a delegated OCSP signing certificate: the CA acts directly as the responder."},"1667":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/ocsp-14","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/ocsp#how-the-responder-works-in-lamassu","content":"Each response has a validity window of 24 hours, reflected in the response's `thisUpdate` and `nextUpdate` fields. Clients that cache responses must take this window into account when determining how long a response remains valid."},"1668":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/ocsp-15","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/ocsp#embedding-in-issued-certificates","content":"The OCSP responder URL is automatically embedded in the AIA (*Authority Information Access*) extension of every certificate issued by Lamassu. Clients that verify certificates can read this URL directly from the certificate without additional configuration."},"1669":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/ocsp-16","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/ocsp#http-endpoints","content":"The responder accepts both formats defined in RFC 6960:"},"1670":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/ocsp-17","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/ocsp#http-endpoints","content":"`GET /ocsp/{ocsp_request}` includes the OCSP request Base64url-encoded within the URL itself."},"1671":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/ocsp-18","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/ocsp#http-endpoints","content":"`POST /ocsp` sends the request in the body with `Content-Type: application/ocsp-request`."},"1672":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/ocsp-19","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/ocsp#http-endpoints","content":"Example query with `curl` using POST:"},"1673":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/ocsp-20","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/ocsp#http-endpoints","content":"The response has `Content-Type: application/ocsp-response` and contains the OCSP response in DER format."},"1674":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/ocsp-21","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/ocsp#check-from-the-interface","content":"From the certificates screen of Lamassu you can launch an OCSP request directly against the selected certificate with the **OCSP Check** action. This action shows the status returned by the responder without needing external tools."},"1675":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/ocsp-22","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/ocsp#references","content":"RFC 6960 - *X.509 Internet Public Key Infrastructure Online Certificate Status Protocol – OCSP*"},"1676":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/ocsp-23","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/ocsp#references","content":"RFC 5280 - *Internet X.509 Public Key Infrastructure Certificate and Certificate Revocation List (CRL) Profile* (revocation reasons, section 5.3.1)"},"1677":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/ocsp-24","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/ocsp#references","content":"<Card title=\"CRL service\" href=\"/docs/platform/pki/crl\" />"},"1678":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/ocsp-25","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/ocsp","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/ocsp#references","content":"<Card title=\"Certificate validation\" href=\"/docs/platform/pki/certificate-validation\" />"},"1679":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/overview","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/overview","type":"page","content":"Lamassu IoT Platform","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Platform"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/overview"},"1680":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/overview-0","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/overview","content":"Manage PKI and digital identities for your devices from a single platform."},"1681":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/overview-1","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/overview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/overview#start-here","content":"Start here"},"1682":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/overview-2","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/overview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/overview#architecture-at-a-glance","content":"Architecture at a glance"},"1683":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/overview-3","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/overview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/overview#core-capabilities","content":"Core capabilities"},"1684":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/overview-4","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/overview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/overview#build-your-trust-hierarchy","content":"Build your trust hierarchy"},"1685":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/overview-5","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/overview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/overview#protect-cryptographic-keys","content":"Protect cryptographic keys"},"1686":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/overview-6","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/overview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/overview#issue-and-control-certificates","content":"Issue and control certificates"},"1687":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/overview-7","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/overview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/overview#automate-device-identities","content":"Automate device identities"},"1688":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/overview-8","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/overview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/overview#publish-validation-status","content":"Publish validation status"},"1689":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/overview-9","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/overview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/overview#react-to-events","content":"React to events"},"1690":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/overview-10","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/overview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/overview#choose-your-path","content":"Choose your path"},"1691":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/overview-11","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/overview","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/overview#operational-reference","content":"Operational reference"},"1692":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/overview-12","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/overview","content":"Lamassu IoT centralizes the issuance, distribution, renewal and revocation of X.509 identities for connected devices. You can build a private PKI, protect its keys and automate the enrollment of a fleet without losing visibility into every certificate."},"1693":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/overview-13","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/overview#start-here","content":"<Card title=\"Get started\" description=\"Create a CA, issue a certificate and register your first device.\" href=\"/docs/platform/pki/quickstarts/overview\" />"},"1694":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/overview-14","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/overview#start-here","content":"<Card title=\"How Lamassu works\" description=\"Build the mental model of authorities, keys, identities and validation.\" href=\"/docs/platform/pki/concepts/overview\" />"},"1695":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/overview-15","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/overview#architecture-at-a-glance","content":"Lamassu runs as a set of services on Kubernetes, backed by PostgreSQL, RabbitMQ and an OIDC provider. Hover a component to trace its connections, or see the platform architecture chapter for the low-level, per-service view."},"1696":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/overview-16","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/overview#build-your-trust-hierarchy","content":"Create root and intermediate authorities or import an existing PKI. Define which authority can issue each identity and keep the full chain of trust."},"1697":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/overview-17","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/overview#protect-cryptographic-keys","content":"Generate and safeguard keys using software engines, PKCS#11 HSMs or cloud services. Lamassu decouples operations from the physical location of the key."},"1698":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/overview-18","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/overview#issue-and-control-certificates","content":"Issue certificates from the console or from a CSR, check their status and revoke them when they stop being trustworthy."},"1699":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/overview-19","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/overview#automate-device-identities","content":"Define enrollment policies with a Device Management Service (DMS) and let devices request or renew their identity through EST."},"1700":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/overview-20","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/overview#publish-validation-status","content":"Offer online validation through OCSP and distribute CRLs for consumers that need to check certificates offline."},"1701":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/overview-21","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/overview#react-to-events","content":"Subscribe to lifecycle changes and send notifications by email, Microsoft Teams or webhooks."},"1702":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/overview-22","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/overview#choose-your-path","content":"<Card title=\"I administer the PKI\" description=\"Configure engines, authorities, issuance and validation.\" href=\"/docs/platform/pki/key-management\" />"},"1703":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/overview-23","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/overview#choose-your-path","content":"<Card title=\"I integrate a device\" description=\"Configure the DMS and use EST to obtain an identity.\" href=\"/docs/platform/pki/device-enrollment\" />"},"1704":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/overview-24","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/overview#choose-your-path","content":"<Card title=\"I operate the platform\" description=\"Deploy Lamassu and prepare its dependencies.\" href=\"/docs/deployment/overview\" />"},"1705":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/overview-25","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-28/platform/pki/overview#choose-your-path","content":"<Card title=\"I integrate another system\" description=\"Connect Lamassu with AWS IoT Core and other des